 "post": {
  "title": "Your Brain Lists What Went Wrong Every Night. Give It the Other List. #shorts",
  "description": "What's one good thing from today? Tell me in the comments. Send this to the friend who replays every mistake. Every night your brain runs the same list: the typo, the weird wave, the text with no emoji. In 'Counting blessings versus burdens' (Journal of Personality and Social Psychology, 2003), Robert Emmons and Michael McCullough had people keep a weekly list for ten weeks: hassles, neutral events, or things they were grateful for. The gratitude group felt better about their lives as a whole, was more optimistic about the coming week, reported fewer physical symptoms and exercised more. Your brain isn't broken; it just never gets asked for the other list. #psychology #shorts #gratitude #overthinking #rumination",
  "tags": [
   "gratitude",
   "overthinking",
   "counting blessings",
   "Emmons McCullough 2003",
   "psychology",
   "can't sleep"
  ]
 },
